    <!-- =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D HOW IT WORKS =3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D -->
    <section class=3D"section section--alt" id=3D"how-it-works" aria-labell=
edby=3D"hiw-title">
      <div class=3D"container">
        <div class=3D"section-header">
          <p class=3D"section-eyebrow">Under the hood</p>
          <h2 id=3D"hiw-title" class=3D"section-title">From plug-in to done=
.</h2>
          <p class=3D"section-desc">Four steps. That's all it takes to back=
 up every file on your Android device.</p>
        </div>

        <div class=3D"steps">
          <div class=3D"step">
            <div class=3D"step-num" aria-hidden=3D"true">01</div>
            <div class=3D"step-content">
              <h3>Install &amp; Grant Root</h3>
              <p>Install the APK and grant Root permissions (via Magisk, Ke=
rnelSU, or APatch) on first launch.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class=3D"step">
            <div class=3D"step-num" aria-hidden=3D"true">02</div>
            <div class=3D"step-content">
              <h3>Phone gets scanned</h3>
              <p>A single <code>find</code> command maps your entire storag=
e in one ADB call =E2=80=94 file paths and sizes. 100,000 files indexed in =
under 10 seconds depending on your device speed.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class=3D"step">
            <div class=3D"step-num" aria-hidden=3D"true">03</div>
            <div class=3D"step-content">
              <h3>You choose what to sync</h3>
              <p>The TreeView GUI opens. Every folder from your phone is li=
sted with lazy-loaded children. Check what you want, uncheck what you don't=
. Or just hit Skip to back up everything.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class=3D"step">
            <div class=3D"step-num" aria-hidden=3D"true">04</div>
            <div class=3D"step-content">
              <h3>Titan Engine fires up</h3>
              <p>Twenty parallel runspaces start pulling. A live progress b=
ar shows throughput in MB/s, total progress, and per-file status. When it's=
 done, the drive unmounts, temp files clean themselves up, and you get a lo=
g.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

